      "keysecondary": [],
      "comment": "Azar: Il Dottore and the god-making plan",
      "content": "Il Dottore, an expelled scholar who became a Fatui Harbinger, returned to Sumeru and offered the sages a new god. Azar and three other sages accepted; Naphis and Baladhuri refused and were imprisoned. Dottore supplied Scaramouche, the Balladeer, as the vessel. In a past scene viewed in Irminsul (3.3), Azar stresses that the biological transformation is slow and that the subject, once linked to the machine, would be unable to move on his own.",
